    "7.13.116: fix: StepRail's bar scale (sumDur/sumTokens) still summed EVERY step including GATE steps (task c5b70c27, third pass). A gate's duration is human approval wait time, not agent work -- on task 292e8ea2, plan_gate sat pending 85h49m while real agent steps (review previous notes, draft story, verify plan, write failing tests, implement tasks) each ran 30s-3min, so the gate's wait time dominated the sum so completely that every real step's bar was crushed to the 2% floor while the gate's own bar read ~100%. Fixed two ways: (1) the sumDur/sumTokens accumulation loop in StepRail now skips steps where s.type === 'gate' entirely, so only real agent work scales the bars; (2) a resolved (non-pending) gate row no longer renders a proportional fill bar at all -- StepMeta gained an isGate prop that guards the `h-2 rounded-full` bar track, and GateRow's resolved-gate call site passes isGate so a gate always renders as plain duration/token caption text, never a pct-based fill (a gate's wait time isn't commensurable with agent work no matter what it's scaled against). Extended tests/unit/test_step_rail_bar_scale_is_total.py with test_gate_wait_time_is_excluded_from_the_bar_scale and test_gate_row_never_renders_a_proportional_bar. "
