    "'pip install prism-service[neural]' log) so default search never loads the "
    "2nd OpenMP runtime; PRISM_RERANK behavior is preserved when neural is "
    "installed. (3) OBSERVABILITY — new brain_engine.log_threadpool_info() logs "
    "threadpoolctl.threadpool_info() at startup (main._configure_logging) AND "
    "after model load so prism.log PROVES pools are pinned to num_threads==1. "
    "Tests: tests/integration/test_embedding_no_deadlock.py (pin-overrides-"
    "preset-env, torch-not-imported on default encode+search, concurrency "
    "no-hang, startup/post-load threadpool_info log). "
    "v6.5.7: The out-of-process supervisor (GH #162) now survives systemd and "
    "waits for a healthy respawn (task d10e4623, hardens v6.5.6). Live "
    "verification under the customer's systemd --user/Linux env exposed two "
    "gaps. GAP 1 (cgroup teardown): cmd_start wrote the SERVER pid as the "
    "systemd Type=simple main pid and ran the supervisor as a SIBLING, so a "
    "supervisor SIGKILL of the wedged server tore the whole cgroup down, "
    "killing the supervisor too. FIX: a new LEAD MODE — `python -m "
    "prism_service.services.supervisor` invoked with NO server-pid arg spawns "
    "the server as its OWN child and supervises it in the FOREGROUND, so "
    "systemd tracks the SUPERVISOR (not the server) as the unit main pid; the "
    "watched server's death/respawn is then invisible to systemd. The proven "
    "`<server_pid> <ui_port>` SIBLING invocation (cmd_start) still works "
    "unchanged (SIGKILL-never-graceful, atomic pidfile rewrite, ~5s wedge "
    "bound). Ships a committed, documented deploy/prism.service (ExecStart=the "
    "supervisor lead mode, Restart=always); systemd-on-Linux end-to-end is a "
    "manual customer step noted in the unit. GAP 2 (mid-boot kill + unbounded "
    "restarts): after EVERY (re)spawn the supervisor now waits for probe_alive "
    "OR a startup_grace_s timeout (default 30s, env PRISM_SUPERVISOR_STARTUP_"
    "GRACE_S) BEFORE any hung probe counts toward a kill — a cold child (model "
    "load ~7-9s) whose boot exceeds probe_interval*failure_threshold is NOT "
    "killed mid-warmup; the grace is RE-APPLIED per respawn (SupervisorState."
    "mark_spawned re-stamps the anchor, _in_startup_grace gates "
    "handle_probe_result), not just first boot. And max_restarts default "
    "changes from 0/unlimited to a FINITE 5 so a genuinely crash-looping child "
    "backs off to systemd (Restart=always) instead of thrashing forever. "
    "Tests: tests/integration/test_supervisor_systemd_lead_respawn_grace.py. "
    "v6.5.6: PRISM auto-recovers from the silent all-threads futex wedge "
    "with NO manual SIGKILL (GH #162, task d180915b; 3rd iteration after "
    "#155/v6.5.0 + #157/v6.5.2). The in-process watchdog CANNOT save the "
    "process: its os._exit(1) self-heal AND its per-cycle faulthandler re-arm "
    "BOTH need the GIL the native-futex holder never yields, so during a true "
    "wedge the watchdog thread is itself parked. THREE changes: (1) NEW "
    "services/supervisor.py — an OUT-OF-PROCESS supervisor launched by `prism "
    "start --daemon` (cli/prism_cli.py cmd_start) as its OWN `python -m "
    "prism_service.services.supervisor <server_pid> <ui_port>` child, off the "
    "server's contended GIL path (a SEPARATE PROCESS, never a thread — a "
    "thread wedges identically). It HTTP-probes /api/version on a ~1s cadence "
    "and, after failure_threshold() consecutive timeouts (~5s bound, vs the "
    "watchdog's 90s), force_kill()s the wedged server with SIGKILL / taskkill "
    "/F (NEVER SIGTERM — graceful drain is itself wedged) and respawn_server()s "
    "it, rewriting the pidfile atomically to the new pid. Knobs mirror the "
    "watchdog tri-state: PRISM_SUPERVISOR(off) / _INTERVAL_S / _FAILURES / "
    "_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S / _MAX_RESTARTS (thundering-herd guard). (2) faulthandler "
    "is now CONTINUOUSLY ARMED in main._configure_logging via "
    "dump_traceback_later(repeat=True) — the C timer free-runs on its own C "
    "thread and re-fires every PRISM_FAULTHANDLER_REPEAT_S (default 30s) even "
    "when every Python thread is parked on the futex, closing the unarmed "
    "window the GIL-bound watchdog _loop left (so a wedge finally emits an "
    "all-thread traceback to prism.log to root-cause + eliminate the deadlock). "
    "(3) the in-process watchdog self-heal PRISM_WATCHDOG_KILL now defaults ON "
    "as defense-in-depth (set =0 to opt out), while the supervisor remains the "
    "actual recovery guarantee. Honest scope: this GUARANTEES auto-recovery + "
    "CAPTURES the stack; it does not by itself claim the futex deadlock is "
    "eliminated. Tests: tests/integration/test_external_supervisor_recovery.py. "
    "v6.5.4: Auto-update no longer strands the daemon on the old build "
    "(task 73ec7273, lineage of GH #66). The restart watcher set "
    "_server.should_exit but NEVER _server.force_exit, so a held-open MCP "
    "streamable-HTTP connection blocked uvicorn's graceful drain forever — "
    ".run() never returned, the main-thread os.execv (the version flip) was "
    "never reached, and the wheel sat on disk while the served version "
    "stranded on the old build. FIX (main.py _restart_watcher): after "
    "should_exit, escalate to force_exit once the drain exceeds "
    "PRISM_RESTART_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_S (default 10s) so uvicorn DROPS the "
    "connection, .run() returns, and the EXISTING main-thread execv fires — "
    "graceful-first, force-after-timeout so in-flight Brain writes/task "
    "mutations get the drain window. auto_updater.perform_restart now honors "
    "its previously-dead drain_timeout_s param the same way. #66 invariants "
    "preserved: execv stays on the MAIN thread, pidfile not unlinked before "
    "the in-place execv. SettingsPage.tsx now shows a loud 'Update ready — "
    "click to restart' control when restart_required is true, turning a "
    "slow/blocked drain into a one-click user action. Tests: "
    "tests/integration/test_auto_update_restart_drain.py. "
