    "v6.5.2: Single-flight Brain embeddings — concurrent encodes can no longer "
    "wedge PRISM (GH #157, task 1b28cde8). v6.5.0 pinned native math to 1 "
    "thread per embed + a deadlock watchdog, but did NOTHING about TWO "
    "concurrent embeds: _MODEL_LOCK (brain_engine.py:153) serializes only the "
    "model LOAD. The three _MODEL.encode() native-inference sites "
    "(encode_task_text ~:90, health probe ~:786, _embed doc-index ~:1161) ran "
    "UNLOCKED, so two request threads (e.g. a Conductor verifier embed + a "
    "concurrent task_update embed) entering model2vec->numpy/BLAS native math "
    "at once inverted the GIL<->native-futex and silently wedged every thread "
    "(ports return curl->000 while systemd still reports active). FIX: a "
    "dedicated module-level _ENCODE_LOCK (distinct from _MODEL_LOCK; no "
    "load-inside-encode nesting) now wraps each encode so only ONE runs at a "
    "time; the `_MODEL is None` / vector_enabled fast-path guards stay OUTSIDE "
    "the lock and the numpy asarray/tolist conversions are kept out of the "
    "critical section to protect throughput. Belt-and-suspenders "
    "_threadpool_limit_1() pins BLAS/OMP to 1 thread around the encode ONLY "
    "when threadpoolctl is importable (optional import, never a hard "
    "dependency). Tests: tests/integration/test_embedding_single_flight.py "
    "(source-asserts all three sites acquire _ENCODE_LOCK + a runtime in-flight "
    "overlap counter that must never exceed 1, deterministic across repeated "
    "runs + correctness). "
    "v6.5.0: Deadlock watchdog + native-math thread guards for the silent "
    "all-threads wedge (GH #155, task 8b231401). #155 = OpenMP/OpenBLAS futex "
    "oversubscription on the embedding path: a request thread enters native "
    "math (model2vec/numpy BLAS) holding the GIL, blocks on a native futex, "
    "and every other Python thread starves on the GIL — total wedge, no "
    "traceback (faulthandler.enable() only fires on a fatal signal). THREE "
    "LAYERS + a UI surface: (1) PREVENT — new prism_service/thread_limits.py "
    "apply_thread_limits() pins OMP/OPENBLAS/MKL/NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=1 + "
    "OMP_WAIT_POLICY=PASSIVE + TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM=false, ONLY for vars "
    "the operator has not set (operator intent wins); imported + invoked at "
    "the VERY TOP of main.py AND cli/prism_cli.py BEFORE the config/brain "
    "import block that transitively pulls numpy. (2) DETECT+CAPTURE — new "
    "services/watchdog.py daemon thread: each cycle ARMS "
    "faulthandler.dump_traceback_later(timeout, repeat=False, file=prism.log) "
    "then runs a REAL in-process HTTP self-probe GET 127.0.0.1:{UI_PORT}/; a "
    "healthy probe cancels the timer + records latency, a HANGING probe does "
    "NOT cancel so the C-level timer fires and dumps ALL thread stacks even "
    "while every Python thread is deadlocked. Status dict (last_probe_ok, "
    "last_probe_latency_ms, consecutive_failures, last_dump_at, dump_count, "
    "restarts) + tunables PRISM_WATCHDOG / PRISM_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_S(~30) / "
    "PRISM_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT_S(~20). (3) RECOVER — opt-in os._exit(1) when "
    "PRISM_WATCHDOG_KILL=1 and consecutive_failures exceeds threshold "
    "(default OFF) so a supervisor restarts the wedged process. (4) SURFACE — "
    "GET /api/watchdog (watchdog_router wired into api/__init__.py like "
    "consolidation_router) + a Diagnostics health card in the SPA with "
    "progressive disclosure (one-line summary + click-to-expand last-dump "
    "excerpt). Watchdog started in main.py lifespan beside the maintenance "
    "clock, stopped on shutdown. Tests: tests/integration/"
    "test_thread_limits_guards.py + test_watchdog_arm_cancel.py + "
    "test_watchdog_api_route.py. "
