    "\n\n7.13.80: found while investigating why a freshly-driven child task "
    "(3a3f90da) sat stuck at story_gate -- a real, systemic rubric-parser "
    "bug, not a story defect. arc_governance.py's _ac_lines and "
    "_claim_lines (story_complete and premise_grounded rubrics) matched "
    "ANY bulleted line as the start of a new entry, with no check on "
    "indentation. A nested '- oracle: ...' or '- <citation>' sub-bullet "
    "written UNDER its parent AC/claim -- the natural, instructed shape, "
    "an indented CHILD bullet, not a same-line suffix -- was matched too, "
    "so it started its own untracked sibling entry instead of folding "
    "into the parent the docstring already claimed it would. Every one "
    "of 3a3f90da's 9 ACs had a correctly-placed nested oracle line and "
    "still read as 100% oracle-less; one nested oracle even got "
    "mis-attributed to a different AC because its own prose happened to "
    "contain that AC's id as a substring. Fixed both functions by "
    "tracking each entry's starting indentation: a bullet only opens a "
    "NEW entry when it is not MORE indented than the entry currently "
    "being built. Two new regression tests (one per function) pin the "
    "nested-bullet case. 124 rubric/gate/premise tests green, including "
    "the real story replayed through the fixed parser (all 9 ACs now "
    "correctly read as having oracles)."
    "\n\n7.13.81: MemoryService._brain_recall dropped every Brain hit on a "
    "sliding-window chunk of a long memory (doc_id ...::win_N) because it "
    "stripped only the literal ::main suffix, so parts[-1] kept the ::win_N "
    "tail and never matched entry_map. Now splits on the first '::' to "
    "strip any chunk suffix, and dedupes multiple chunk hits for the same "
    "entry_id so one long memory's windows do not crowd out other results. "
    "New tests/unit/test_memory_recall_window_chunks.py pins both; 5/5 "
    "green, neighbouring recall/activation-score/private-memory suites "
    "unaffected."
    "\n\n7.13.82: mitigated a Claude Code HARNESS bug that hit implement.js "
    "step subagents twice in one real session -- a step's Bash tool went "
    "unconditionally blocked mid-step with 'This session is isolated in "
    "the worktree <some worktree>, but this command's working directory "
    "resolved to the shared checkout... Refusing to run it there', naming "
    "a worktree that belonged to a DIFFERENT, sibling agent (once the MAIN "
    "session itself) -- never one the blocked subagent was ever told to "
    "use. ExitWorktree refused to help too ('cannot be called from a "
    "subagent with a cwd override... already isolated'), so the subagent "
    "was structurally unable to clear it itself. This is a platform/harness "
    "bug (filed separately as platform feedback), not a PRISM or task "
    "defect and not root-cause-fixable from this repo -- so the fix here "
    "is PRISM-side mitigation only. Added a new ENV_COLLISION_DOCTRINE "
    "constant naming the exact refusal signature, forbidding any clever "
    "workaround (no retry via another tool, no self-clearing the isolation "
    "state), and instructing an immediate clean stop reported as ok:false "
    "with halt_reason carrying the fixed, greppable prefix 'ENVIRONMENT "
    "COLLISION (cwd-isolation leak): ' -- so the next reader (human or "
    "orchestrator) can tell at a glance this needs a fresh relaunch, never "
    "a content fix, without reconstructing it from a generic failure "
    "paragraph. Recovery is explicitly a FRESH relaunch once no other "
    "agent in the session is mid-EnterWorktree, never resumeFromRunId (per "
    "this file's own existing never-resumeFromRunId rule -- cached "
    "pre-flight verdicts replay stale). Injected into SELF_HEAL (reaches "
    "every workerPrompt/decompose/child-driver/locate/graph/settle agent "
    "via preamble()) AND directly into gatePrompt, which builds its prompt "
    "standalone and does not call preamble() at all. Checked whether any "
    "agent() call passed Claude Code's OWN isolation:'worktree' option "
    "(would add unnecessary surface area for this exact collision, since "
    "every step already runs inside PRISM's own separate task_workspace "
    "git-worktree mechanism) -- none do, so no removal was needed there. "
    "New regression test (test_implement_env_collision_doctrine.py, 6 "
    "cases) pins the doctrine text, its injection into both SELF_HEAL and "
    "gatePrompt, the fixed halt prefix, and the never-resumeFromRunId "
    "recovery instruction. 149 implement.js-adjacent tests green."
